  "summary": "Ardmore, Oklahoma city commissioners are responding to phase two of a recall petition drive tied to their approval of Flock police surveillance cameras. Mayor David Plesher said he is open to letting voters decide the fate of the Flock contract at a September 21 meeting, and walked back an earlier statement about bagging the cameras pending a February vote.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Our streets are public streets, and there's no privacy on public streets\u2026 period",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "I'm okay with giving the people the vote on it",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "If the people decide that they want them pulled down, then we will do it at that time",
      "paragraph_idx": 19
    }
